IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uro-nouns`

-- Social Security Benefits Up-rating Order 2026 (S.I. 2026/148): PART 2, ARTICLE 7.
-- Layer 1. Article 7 gives the dates on which the changes in articles 3, 4, 5, 6, 11, 12 and 13 take effect
-- "for each case" (art 1(5) sends the reader here). Each paragraph (2) to (11) is a rule of its own; the first
-- rule below, for paragraph (1), picks the paragraph for a given kind of sum.
-- Only paragraph (9) depends on the beneficiary: "benefit week" there has "the same meaning as in regulation 2(1)
-- of the Computation of Earnings Regulations" (outside the text), so the first day of the beneficiary's first
-- benefit week is a plain input DATE. Paragraph (1) says (7) "is subject to the provisions of paragraph (9)";
-- (9) concerns only the article 25(b) sum, so the reading taken is that (9) displaces (7) for that sum alone
-- (NOTES.md, fork F-03).

§ `Article 7 -- Dates on which sums specified for rates or amounts of benefits in articles 3, 4, 5, 6, 11, 12 and 13 are changed by this Order`

§§ `Article 7(2) to (8), (10) and (11) -- fixed dates`

-- src:99 | (2) Any increases in the sums mentioned in articles 3, 4, 11 and 12 for Category A, Category B, Category C and Category D retirement pension and graduated retirement benefit together with, where appropriate, any increases for dependants, shall take effect on 6th April 2026.
@ref art 7(2) (src:99)
`art 7(2): the date on which the changes take effect for Category A, B, C and D retirement pension and graduated retirement benefit, with increases for dependants` MEANS YMD 2026 4 6

-- src:100 | (3) The increases in the sums mentioned in article 5 shall take effect on 6th April 2026.
@ref art 7(3) (src:100)
`art 7(3): the date on which the increases in the sums mentioned in article 5 take effect` MEANS YMD 2026 4 6

-- src:101 | (4) Any increases in the sums specified for the rate of—
-- src:102 | (a) attendance allowance; and
-- src:104 | shall take effect on 6th April 2026.
@ref art 7(4)(a) (src:101-104)
`art 7(4)(a): the date on which the increase in the rate of attendance allowance takes effect` MEANS YMD 2026 4 6

-- src:101 | (4) Any increases in the sums specified for the rate of—
-- src:103 | (b) carer’s allowance (except in a case where the Secretary of State has made arrangements for it to be paid on a Wednesday),
-- src:104 | shall take effect on 6th April 2026.
@ref art 7(4)(b) (src:101-104)
`art 7(4)(b): the date on which the increase in the rate of carer's allowance takes effect, except where it is paid on a Wednesday` MEANS YMD 2026 4 6

-- src:105 | (5) Any increases in the sums specified for—
-- src:106 | (a) the rate of—
-- src:107 | (i) carer’s allowance in a case where the Secretary of State has made arrangements for it to be paid on a Wednesday;
-- src:115 | shall take effect on 8th April 2026.
@ref art 7(5)(a)(i) (src:105-115)
`art 7(5)(a)(i): the date on which the increase in the rate of carer's allowance takes effect where it is paid on a Wednesday` MEANS YMD 2026 4 8

-- (5)(a)(ii) to (v) and (b)(i), (ii) are dated by the same words of the same paragraph.
-- src:105 | (5) Any increases in the sums specified for—
-- src:108 | (ii) disablement benefit;
-- src:109 | (iii) maximum disablement gratuity under paragraph 9(2) of Schedule 7 to the Contributions and Benefits Act;
-- src:110 | (iv) industrial death benefit by way of widow’s and widower’s pension; and
-- src:111 | (v) the maximum of the aggregate of weekly benefit payable for successive accidents, under section 107(1) of the Contributions and Benefits Act; and
-- src:112 | (b) any increases in—
-- src:113 | (i) the benefit referred to in paragraph (ii) of sub-paragraph (a) in respect of dependants; and
-- src:114 | (ii) disablement pension,
-- src:115 | shall take effect on 8th April 2026.
@ref art 7(5) (src:105-115)
`art 7(5): the date on which the increases for disablement benefit, the maximum disablement gratuity, widow's and widower's industrial death benefit, the maximum aggregate for successive accidents, and disablement benefit and pension for dependants take effect` MEANS YMD 2026 4 8

-- src:116 | (6) In any case where a person’s weekly rate of Category A or Category B retirement pension falls to be increased under the provisions of section 47(1) or 48C(2) of the Contributions and Benefits Act by reference to the weekly rate of invalidity allowance or age addition to long-term incapacity benefit to which the person was previously entitled, any increase in such sum shall take effect on 6th April 2026.
@ref art 7(6) (src:116)
`art 7(6): the date on which the increase in a Category A or B retirement pension by reference to invalidity allowance or age addition takes effect` MEANS YMD 2026 4 6

-- src:117 | (7) The changes in the sums specified for the rate of incapacity benefit and severe disablement allowance together with, where appropriate, any increases for dependants, shall take effect on 9th April 2026.
@ref art 7(7) (src:117)
`art 7(7): the date on which the changes in the rate of incapacity benefit and severe disablement allowance, with increases for dependants, take effect` MEANS YMD 2026 4 9

-- src:118 | (8) The increases in the sums falling to be calculated in accordance with paragraph 13(4) of Schedule 7 to the Contributions and Benefits Act (retirement allowance) shall take effect on 8th April 2026.
@ref art 7(8) (src:118)
`art 7(8): the date on which the increases in the retirement allowance sums take effect` MEANS YMD 2026 4 8

-- src:123 | (10) Any increases in the sums mentioned in article 6 for state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act shall take effect on 6th April 2026.
@ref art 7(10) (src:123)
`art 7(10): the date on which the increases in the sums for state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act take effect` MEANS YMD 2026 4 6

-- src:124 | (11) The increase in the sum mentioned in article 13 shall take effect on 6th April 2026.
@ref art 7(11) (src:124)
`art 7(11): the date on which the increase in the maximum additional pension takes effect` MEANS YMD 2026 4 6

§§ `Article 7(4)(b) and (5)(a)(i) -- carer's allowance`

-- out of text: the Secretary of State's arrangement to pay carer's allowance on a Wednesday is an input.
@ref art 7(4)(b) and (5)(a)(i) (src:101-115)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has made arrangements for it to be paid on a Wednesday` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`art 7(4)(b), (5)(a)(i): the date on which the increase in the rate of carer's allowance takes effect` `the Secretary of State has made arrangements for it to be paid on a Wednesday` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State has made arrangements for it to be paid on a Wednesday`
    THEN `art 7(5)(a)(i): the date on which the increase in the rate of carer's allowance takes effect where it is paid on a Wednesday`
    ELSE `art 7(4)(b): the date on which the increase in the rate of carer's allowance takes effect, except where it is paid on a Wednesday`

§§ `Article 7(9) -- the earnings limit for an adult dependant`

-- out of text: Social Security Benefit (Computation of Earnings) Regulations 1996 reg 7(b) and reg 2(1) ('benefit week'): whether reg 7(b) applies and the first day of the first benefit week are inputs.
-- "(a) except in a case where sub-paragraph (b) applies, on the first day of the first benefit week to commence
-- for the beneficiary on or after 6th April 2026; and (b) in a case where regulation 7(b) of the Computation of
-- Earnings Regulations (date on which earnings are treated as paid) applies, on the first day of the first benefit
-- week to commence for the beneficiary on or after 1st April 2026". A first day before the threshold cannot be
-- the first day of such a week: NOTHING.
-- src:119 | (9) Any increase in the sum specified in article 25(b) of this Order, in so far as that sum is relevant for the purposes of establishing whether the rate of any benefit is not to be increased in respect of an adult dependant because the earnings of the dependant exceed a specified amount, shall take effect—
-- src:120 | (a) except in a case where sub-paragraph (b) applies, on the first day of the first benefit week to commence for the beneficiary on or after 6th April 2026; and
-- src:121 | (b) in a case where regulation 7(b) of the Computation of Earnings Regulations (date on which earnings are treated as paid) applies, on the first day of the first benefit week to commence for the beneficiary on or after 1st April 2026,
-- src:122 | and for the purpose of this paragraph, “benefit week” has the same meaning as in regulation 2(1) of the Computation of Earnings Regulations.
@ref art 7(9) (src:119-122)
GIVEN `regulation 7(b) of the Computation of Earnings Regulations applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of the beneficiary's first benefit week to commence on or after the date in art 7(9)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`art 7(9): the date on which the increase in the article 25(b) sum takes effect for the beneficiary` `regulation 7(b) of the Computation of Earnings Regulations applies` `the first day of the beneficiary's first benefit week to commence on or after the date in art 7(9)` MEANS
    IF `the first day of the beneficiary's first benefit week to commence on or after the date in art 7(9)`
       AT LEAST (IF `regulation 7(b) of the Computation of Earnings Regulations applies` THEN YMD 2026 4 1 ELSE YMD 2026 4 6)
    THEN JUST `the first day of the beneficiary's first benefit week to commence on or after the date in art 7(9)`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Article 7(1) -- which paragraph dates which sum`

-- src:97 | 7 Dates on which sums specified for rates or amounts of benefits in articles 3, 4, 5, 6, 11, 12 and 13 are changed by this Order
-- src:98 | (1) Paragraph (7), which is subject to the provisions of paragraph (9), and paragraphs (2) to (6), (8), (10) and (11) specify the date on which the changes made by this Order in the sums specified for rates or amounts of benefit in articles 3, 4, 5, 6, 11, 12 and 13 shall take effect for each case.
@ref art 7(1) (src:97-98)
DECLARE `a change that art 7 dates` IS ONE OF
    `the change in the sums for Category A, B, C and D retirement pension and graduated retirement benefit, with increases for dependants`
    `the change in the sums mentioned in article 5`
    `the change in the rate of attendance allowance`
    `the change in the rate of carer's allowance`
    `the change in the rate of disablement benefit, the maximum disablement gratuity, widow's and widower's industrial death benefit, the maximum aggregate for successive accidents, and disablement benefit and pension for dependants`
    `the increase in a Category A or B retirement pension by reference to invalidity allowance or age addition to long-term incapacity benefit`
    `the change in the rate of incapacity benefit and severe disablement allowance, with increases for dependants`
    `the increase in the retirement allowance sums`
    `the increase in the article 25(b) sum, so far as it is relevant to the adult dependant earnings test`
    `the increase in the sums for state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act`
    `the increase in the maximum additional pension`

-- out of text: Social Security Benefit (Computation of Earnings) Regulations 1996 reg 7(b) and reg 2(1) (art 7(9)); the Secretary of State's arrangement to pay carer's allowance on a Wednesday (art 7(4)(b), (5)(a)(i)): whether each applies, and the first day of the first benefit week, are inputs.
@ref art 7(1) (src:97-124)
GIVEN `which change` IS A `a change that art 7 dates`
      `the Secretary of State has made arrangements for it to be paid on a Wednesday` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 7(b) of the Computation of Earnings Regulations applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of the beneficiary's first benefit week to commence on or after the date in art 7(9)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`art 7: the date on which the change takes effect` `which change` `the Secretary of State has made arrangements for it to be paid on a Wednesday` `regulation 7(b) of the Computation of Earnings Regulations applies` `the first day of the beneficiary's first benefit week to commence on or after the date in art 7(9)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which change`
    WHEN `the change in the sums for Category A, B, C and D retirement pension and graduated retirement benefit, with increases for dependants` THEN JUST (`art 7(2): the date on which the changes take effect for Category A, B, C and D retirement pension and graduated retirement benefit, with increases for dependants`)
    WHEN `the change in the sums mentioned in article 5` THEN JUST (`art 7(3): the date on which the increases in the sums mentioned in article 5 take effect`)
    WHEN `the change in the rate of attendance allowance` THEN JUST (`art 7(4)(a): the date on which the increase in the rate of attendance allowance takes effect`)
    WHEN `the change in the rate of carer's allowance` THEN JUST (`art 7(4)(b), (5)(a)(i): the date on which the increase in the rate of carer's allowance takes effect` `the Secretary of State has made arrangements for it to be paid on a Wednesday`)
    WHEN `the change in the rate of disablement benefit, the maximum disablement gratuity, widow's and widower's industrial death benefit, the maximum aggregate for successive accidents, and disablement benefit and pension for dependants` THEN JUST (`art 7(5): the date on which the increases for disablement benefit, the maximum disablement gratuity, widow's and widower's industrial death benefit, the maximum aggregate for successive accidents, and disablement benefit and pension for dependants take effect`)
    WHEN `the increase in a Category A or B retirement pension by reference to invalidity allowance or age addition to long-term incapacity benefit` THEN JUST (`art 7(6): the date on which the increase in a Category A or B retirement pension by reference to invalidity allowance or age addition takes effect`)
    WHEN `the change in the rate of incapacity benefit and severe disablement allowance, with increases for dependants` THEN JUST (`art 7(7): the date on which the changes in the rate of incapacity benefit and severe disablement allowance, with increases for dependants, take effect`)
    WHEN `the increase in the retirement allowance sums` THEN JUST (`art 7(8): the date on which the increases in the retirement allowance sums take effect`)
    WHEN `the increase in the article 25(b) sum, so far as it is relevant to the adult dependant earnings test` THEN `art 7(9): the date on which the increase in the article 25(b) sum takes effect for the beneficiary` `regulation 7(b) of the Computation of Earnings Regulations applies` `the first day of the beneficiary's first benefit week to commence on or after the date in art 7(9)`
    WHEN `the increase in the sums for state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act` THEN JUST (`art 7(10): the date on which the increases in the sums for state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act take effect`)
    WHEN `the increase in the maximum additional pension` THEN JUST (`art 7(11): the date on which the increase in the maximum additional pension takes effect`)
